WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.622
The choice between a list and a tuple depends on how you expect the data to behave.

00:00:05.622 --> 00:00:10.462
Use a list when values may be added, removed, sorted, or updated.

00:00:10.462 --> 00:00:19.062
Use a tuple when the values form a fixed record or when you want to return several results that belong together.

00:00:19.873 --> 00:00:26.165
A simple rule is: lists are flexible collections; tuples are fixed records.

00:00:26.165 --> 00:00:29.490
That rule will cover many beginner use cases.
